<title>USA: FGIC qualifies seven issues for bond insurance.</title>
<headline>FGIC qualifies seven issues for bond insurance.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Financial Guaranty Insurance Co. said on Wednesday that it qualified for bond insurance the following seven municipal bond issues scheduled for competitive sale today.</p>
<p>--Berkeley, Calif., $10.5 million GO bonds.</p>
<p>--Pleasanton USD, Calif., $8.685 million and $7.315 million of GO bonds.</p>
<p>--Chatham, Mass., $10 million GO bonds.</p>
<p>--Massachusetts Bay Transportation Authority $200 million of general transportation bonds.</p>
<p>--Albuquerque, N.M., $46.715 million of water and sewer bonds.</p>
<p>--William Floyd UFSD, N.Y., $12.9 million of school district bonds. --U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
</text>
